WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.313
If the agency does run its
own servers, which ones?

2
00:00:03.313 --> 00:00:08.787
Where its DNS runs on an Infoblox
Grid, vNIOS is the natural choice.

3
00:00:08.787 --> 00:00:12.712
It joins the same Grid and takes
its policy from the Grid Master.

4
00:00:12.712 --> 00:00:18.288
One caution: vNIOS failover in GovCloud
and Azure Government is a point to confirm.

5
00:00:18.288 --> 00:00:20.744
BIND is the choice when there's no Grid,

6
00:00:20.744 --> 00:00:24.388
for a small footprint, or when
a tool expects BIND itself.

7
00:00:24.388 --> 00:00:27.994
BIND has no policy plane
of its own; for Book 08,

8
00:00:27.994 --> 00:00:31.699
its policy comes from
the DDI platform and Git.

9
00:00:31.699 --> 00:00:32.688
Which BIND?

10
00:00:32.688 --> 00:00:36.713
ISC supports each even-numbered
branch for four years.

11
00:00:36.713 --> 00:00:42.517
As of October twenty-ninth, 9.20 is
the supported production branch,

12
00:00:42.517 --> 00:00:47.900
with end of life in 2028, and 9.18
reached end of life in June 2026.

13
00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:52.940
Operating-system packages follow their
vendor, so record which support you rely on.
